Package: BMZDP
Title: Bayesian Semi-Parametric Joint Model for Clustered Zero-Inflated Recurrent Events and a Terminal Event
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Xinyuan", "Tian", email = "x.tian@yale.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Markov chain Monte Carlo sampler for the BMZ-DP model of Tian et al.
    (2024), which jointly models a zero-inflated recurrent event process and a
    terminal event process for clustered data. The recurrent intensity is a
    point-mass mixture of non-homogeneous Poisson processes, shared random
    effects link the recurrent and terminal event processes, and Dirichlet
    process priors are placed on the residual of the accelerated failure time
    model for the terminal event and on the cluster-specific frailty
    distribution.
